cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or the ideas in it, please cite the paper."
title: "The Steering Budget: Examples beat Knobs"
authors:
  - family-names: Rajendran
    given-names: Raj Kumar
repository-code: "https://github.com/rajkumars-work/steering"
abstract: >-
  How far a generative model can be steered on a labeled property is fixed,
  before training, by a budget read off the training data. The budget splits
  into a within-category part a knob can reach and a between-category part it
  cannot; composing examples ("showing") reaches the second part, which a knob
  ("telling") structurally cannot. Verified in image and crystal-structure
  generation.
keywords:
  - generative models
  - steering
  - diffusion models
  - crystal structure generation
  - law of total variance
license: MIT
